meta {
  name: Send the register again
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/attendance/register
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "subject_offering_id": "{{offeringId}}",
    "period_id": "{{periodOneId}}",
    "attendance_date": "2026-11-02",
    "source": "manual",
    "entries": [
      {
        "student_id": "{{studentId}}",
        "status": "late",
        "reason_code": "TRANSPORT",
        "remarks": "School bus held up at the level crossing."
      }
    ]
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.created: eq 0
  res.body.updated: eq 1
  res.body.marks[0].status: eq late
  res.body.marks[0].reason_code: eq TRANSPORT
}

docs {
  The same pupil, the same date, the same period: an upsert on the natural key
  rather than a second row. created drops to 0 and updated rises to 1, which
  is how a client tells "I corrected the register" from "I took it twice".

  This is what makes the route safe to retry. A teacher whose phone lost
  signal halfway through can send the whole register again without creating
  duplicates or having to work out which pupils got through.

  reason_code is a short school-defined string, 64 characters at most. It is
  not validated against a list, because the list differs per school and a
  refused code would lose the mark along with the reason.
}
